{"id":"system-wide","window":["2016-10-24","2022-12-30"],"cells_tested":174,"cells_pass_bh":3,"cells_expected_by_chance":0.3,"intro":["One panel of 46,167 instrument-sessions (34 instruments, Oct 2017 to Dec 2022; 9,527 on the 7 USD majors with the dollar share), every input known before the session: σ position (percentile of σ in its last 252 sessions), forecast error, C.OG's turbulent regime, own and market-wide bursts the session before, and the dollar share. Outcomes: the session range and a 1σ stop from the open on the M1 bid/ask path. 2023 onward is not looked at.","The layers are mostly separate inputs, not one thing measured several ways: 9 outputs behave like 5.3 independent ones (8.8 if shifted out of time with each other, 1 if one thing). The overlap is all on the σ side: σ position and σ vs long-run correlate 0.97, P(high regime) 0.67 with σ. Error, bursts and the dollar share sit near 0 with everything.","And they add: out of sample (2019-2022) all five together remove 6.9% of the squared error of the log range against 6.7% for the sum of each alone, and 4.1% vs 4.1% for the stop. Forecast error does most (4.0%), then σ position (2.4%, the over-reaction), regime 0.2%, market-wide burst 0.1%, own burst ~0. The dollar share makes the forecast worse out of sample (−0.3%): it describes risk, it does not move the range.","No pair interacts beyond adding. Of 15 pairs, 3 beat their own shuffled product on the range and 2 on the stop, about what chance gives; the largest gain is +0.08% of squared error with an interval across 0. Regime × dollar share overfits (−0.5 to −0.8%). Across 174 cells, 3 pass Benjamini-Hochberg (0.3 expected false), and none is an interaction: they are the error alone in calm (+6.1pp stop hits, top vs bottom third) and turbulent regimes (+4.9pp), and the London-open timing.","The best-looking pair, σ position × market-wide burst yesterday (+3.2pp on the stop [−0.2, +6.1]), is too noisy to tell and fails Lesson 01: one session more delay flips it to −2.5pp, a 3-session burst look-back gives −0.1pp, 2018 and 2020 and the indices go the other way.","Agreement matters because the layers add: when 3+ point loud and none quiet the 1σ bid/ask stop is hit 42% of the time (n=326, range 1.91σ); when they agree quiet, 22% (1.29σ); when they disagree, 30% (1.55σ), against 32% for all sessions and 29% on mid (the spread adds about 3pp).","C.OG's regime: 95 turbulent episodes, median 63 sessions, 15% of sessions. The error's effect holds across both regimes; no layer pair changes inside the regime beyond noise. Stops are first touched most in the 13-16 London overlap.","For the system: size and stop width can take the layers as a sum (σ × error feedback × an over-reaction haircut, plus a small burst add-on), with no product terms. Product terms are where the overfitting lives."],"holds":[{"effect":"Layers are mostly separate inputs","where":"7 majors (9 outputs) and all 34 (8 outputs), 2018-2022","size":"effective inputs 5.3 of 9 (majors), 5.1 of 8 (all 34)","benchmark":"time-shuffled 8.8 / 8.0; one thing = 1"},{"effect":"Forecast error is the layer that moves next session's range","where":"all 34, walk-forward 2019-2022","size":"3.97% of squared log-range error alone; all five 6.93%","benchmark":"instrument means = 0; sum of the five alone 6.74%"},{"effect":"Best pair on the stop: σ position × market-wide burst yday","where":"pooled, walk-forward 2019-2022","size":"interaction gain +0.011% [-0.035, +0.061], contrast +3.2pp [-0.2, +6.1]","benchmark":"shuffled a×b 95th pct +0.006%"},{"effect":"Best pair on the range","where":"pooled, walk-forward 2019-2022","size":"σ position × forecast error +0.082% [-0.415, +0.620]","benchmark":"shuffled a×b 95th pct +0.005%"},{"effect":"Agreement of the layers","where":"all 34, Oct 2017-2022","size":"stop hit agree-loud 42.2%, agree-quiet 22.3%, disagree 29.9%","benchmark":"all sessions 32.2%"}],"charts":[{"type":"groups","title":"How correlated are the layer outputs? Rank correlation, 7 USD majors, 2018-2022","names":["S σ position","E forecast error","R turbulent","D dollar share"],"unit":"correlation","note":"Each row is one layer output; the four columns are its correlation with σ position, forecast error, the turbulent regime and the dollar share (ranks within instrument, 9,079 sessions). Look for anything far from 0 off the diagonal: σ position and σ vs long-run are one thing (0.97), P(high regime) and the turbulent regime lean on σ (0.40-0.69); error, bursts and dollar share sit near 0 with everything. Benchmark: the same columns circularly shifted in time are 0. Effective number of independent inputs (participation ratio of the eigenvalues): 5.3 of 9 here and 5.1 of 8 on all 34 instruments, against 8.8 and 8.0 when the columns are shifted out of time with each other, and 1 if they were one thing; Nyholt M_eff 8.3.","rows":[{"label":"σ position","values":[1.0,0.067,0.402,0.186]},{"label":"σ vs long-run","values":[0.973,0.04,0.489,0.215]},{"label":"forecast error","values":[0.067,1.0,-0.169,0.084]},{"label":"P(high regime)","values":[0.672,0.138,0.498,0.367]},{"label":"turbulent regime","values":[0.402,-0.169,1.0,0.392]},{"label":"dollar share","values":[0.186,0.084,0.392,1.0]},{"label":"own burst yday","values":[0.009,0.013,-0.024,-0.014]},{"label":"market-wide burst yday","values":[0.046,0.046,0.028,0.04]},{"label":"burst intensity","values":[0.091,-0.07,-0.093,-0.22]}]},{"type":"groups","title":"Each layer alone vs all together: out-of-sample gain over instrument means, 2019-2022","names":["session range (log range/σ)","1σ stop hit, bid/ask"],"unit":"% of squared error removed","note":"Walk-forward by year (fit on earlier years, score the next). Look at the last two rows: if the layers were one thing measured several ways, 'all together' would be far below the 'sum of alone'; if separate, close to it. Range: all five 6.93% vs sum alone 6.74%. Benchmark: instrument means only = 0; a shuffled input scores ≤ 0.","rows":[{"label":"σ position","values":[2.41,1.85]},{"label":"forecast error","values":[3.97,2.0]},{"label":"turbulent regime","values":[0.21,0.2]},{"label":"own burst yday","values":[0.02,0.02]},{"label":"market-wide burst yday","values":[0.13,0.06]},{"label":"dollar share (majors)","values":[-0.34,-0.19]},{"label":"sum of the five alone","values":[6.74,4.14]},{"label":"all five together","values":[6.93,4.14]}]},{"type":"groups","title":"Does the pair interact? Out-of-sample gain of a×b beyond a+b, session range, 2019-2022","names":["interaction gain","shuffled a×b, 95th pct"],"unit":"% of additive model's squared error","note":"Each row adds the product of two layers to a model that already has both alone (plus instrument means). A real interaction must beat the 95th percentile of the same product with one layer circularly shifted in time (60 draws). Rows with the dollar share are majors only. Values in hundredths of a percent are noise-sized.","rows":[{"label":"σ position × forecast error","values":[0.082,0.005]},{"label":"σ position × market-wide burst yday","values":[0.039,0.003]},{"label":"forecast error × dollar share","values":[0.013,0.096]},{"label":"σ position × turbulent regime","values":[0.012,0.021]},{"label":"σ position × own burst yday","values":[0.004,0.001]},{"label":"own burst yday × market-wide burst yday","values":[0.0,0.005]},{"label":"turbulent regime × own burst yday","values":[-0.013,0.004]},{"label":"forecast error × own burst yday","values":[-0.016,0.004]},{"label":"forecast error × turbulent regime","values":[-0.018,0.008]},{"label":"dollar share × own burst yday","values":[-0.031,0.019]},{"label":"turbulent regime × market-wide burst yday","values":[-0.04,0.001]},{"label":"dollar share × market-wide burst yday","values":[-0.052,0.051]},{"label":"forecast error × market-wide burst yday","values":[-0.061,0.001]},{"label":"σ position × dollar share","values":[-0.088,-0.005]},{"label":"turbulent regime × dollar share","values":[-0.798,0.025]}]},{"type":"groups