error alone (top − bottom third), calm","value":6.11,"lo":5.03,"hi":7.15},{"label":"forecast error alone (top − bottom third), turbulent","value":4.89,"lo":3.27,"hi":6.52}]},{"type":"groups","title":"Time of day: share of 1σ bid/ask stops first touched in each London bucket, by σ position × market-wide burst yday","names":["both high","both low","one high one low"],"unit":"% of stops (long and short)","note":"Europe/London clock. Shows WHEN the extra stops arrive when both layers point loud, against both quiet and the split case. Benchmark: the all-sessions share per bucket is in the table's last column (fourth value). Buckets sum to the session's hit rate.","rows":[{"label":"Asia 00-07","values":[5.36,5.55,3.63]},{"label":"London open 07-10","values":[5.84,8.26,5.26]},{"label":"London mid 10-13","values":[4.87,6.22,4.85]},{"label":"Overlap 13-16","values":[8.71,10.57,8.89]},{"label":"NY pm 16-22","values":[6.88,6.02,5.99]}]},{"type":"bars","title":"By horizon and price: interaction contrast of σ position × market-wide burst yday","unit":"pp (stops) or σ-units (range)","ref":0,"note":"Stops in percentage points, ranges in log units (this session) or σ (5-session mean). Gross (mid) vs net (bid/ask, one spread) shows whether the spread changes the picture. Benchmark 0 = the layers add.","rows":[{"label":"stop hit, mid (gross)","value":2.621,"lo":-0.611,"hi":5.574},{"label":"stop hit, bid/ask (net)","value":3.159,"lo":-0.158,"hi":6.07},{"label":"log range/σ, this session","value":0.064,"lo":0.005,"hi":0.117},{"label":"range/σ, mean of 5 sessions","value":-0.011,"lo":-0.078,"hi":0.049}]},{"type":"bars","title":"+1 session lag check: every input delayed one more session","unit":"% of squared error removed (gains) or pp (contrast)","ref":0,"note":"C.OG Lesson 01: an effect that is real should survive a one-session delay with a smaller size, not vanish or flip. Shown for the headline interaction and for the strongest single layer (forecast error alone). Benchmarks: the shu